IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 12: Scope of Acts and statutory instruments (ss 120 to 122).
--
-- s 120 keeps an Act within the legislative power of the Assembly, s 121 says whom an Act binds, s 122 says which entity or place a name in an Act refers to.
-- Whether an interpretation exceeds the power, and whether a requirement is for the payment of money forming part of the public money of the Territory,
-- are judgements the text leaves to the reader; the rules below take each as a plain input.
-- ss 120 (5) and 121 (5) say the sections are determinative provisions; that is in `act-determinative.l4`.
--
-- A rule that says "is not affected" or "does not bind" answers JUST FALSE where its condition holds.
-- A rule whose condition fails answers NOTHING, because the text does not say what happens then.
-- A "means" or "is authorised if" definition answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE for the kinds of entity it names.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 12, Scope of Acts and statutory instruments`

§§ `Section 120: Act to be interpreted not to exceed legislative powers of Assembly`

-- src:1571 | (1) An Act is to be interpreted as operating to the full extent of, but not to exceed, the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly.
@ref s 120 (1) (src:1571-1571)
GIVEN theInterpretationOperatesToTheFullExtentOfTheLegislativePower IS A BOOLEAN, theInterpretationExceedsTheLegislativePower IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120 (1): the interpretation of the Act is the one the section directs` MEANS
    IF   theInterpretationExceedsTheLegislativePower
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF   theInterpretationOperatesToTheFullExtentOfTheLegislativePower
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1572 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a provision of an Act would, apart from this section, be interpreted as exceeding the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly—
@ref s 120 (2) opening words (src:1572-1572)
-- src:1573 | (a) the provision is valid to the extent to which it does not exceed power; and
@ref s 120 (2) (a) (src:1573-1573)
GIVEN theProvisionWouldApartFromThisSectionBeInterpretedAsExceedingThePower IS A BOOLEAN, thisPartOfTheProvisionExceedsThePower IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120 (2) (a): the provision is effective as to the part` MEANS
    IF   NOT theProvisionWouldApartFromThisSectionBeInterpretedAsExceedingThePower
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   thisPartOfTheProvisionExceedsThePower
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1572 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a provision of an Act would, apart from this section, be interpreted as exceeding the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly—
@ref s 120 (2) opening words (src:1572-1572)
-- src:1574 | (b) the remainder of the Act is not affected.
@ref s 120 (2) (b) (src:1574-1574)
GIVEN theProvisionWouldApartFromThisSectionBeInterpretedAsExceedingThePower IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120 (2) (b): the remainder of the Act is affected` MEANS
    IF   theProvisionWouldApartFromThisSectionBeInterpretedAsExceedingThePower
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1575 | (3) Without limiting subsection (1), if the application of a provision of an Act to a matter would, apart from this section, be interpreted as exceeding power, the provision’s application to other matters is not affected.
@ref s 120 (3) (src:1575-1575)
GIVEN theApplicationToTheMatterWouldApartFromThisSectionBeInterpretedAsExceedingThePower IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120 (3): the provision's application to other matters is affected` MEANS
    IF   theApplicationToTheMatterWouldApartFromThisSectionBeInterpretedAsExceedingThePower
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1576 | (4) This section is in addition to any provision of the Act itself.
-- src:1577 | Note For the equivalent provision for statutory instruments, see s 43.
@ref s 120 (4) (src:1576-1577)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 120 (4): this section is in addition to any provision of the Act itself` MEANS TRUE

§§ `Section 121: Binding effect of Acts`

-- The five governments named in the definition of government in s 121 (6), and the persons s 121 (1) names.
-- `anyone or anything else` stands for any subject the text does not name.
-- src:1582 | (1) An Act binds everyone, including people who are not Australian citizens and all governments.
@ref s 121 (1) (src:1582-1582)
-- src:1595 | government includes the Territory, the Commonwealth, a State, another Territory or New Zealand.
@ref s 121 (6), definition of government (src:1595-1595)
DECLARE `Who or what an Act is applied to` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `a person who is not an Australian citizen`
    `the Territory (as a government)`
    `the Commonwealth (as a government)`
    `a State (as a government)`
    `another Territory (as a government)`
    `New Zealand (as a government)`
    `anyone or anything else`

-- src:1595 | government includes the Territory, the Commonwealth, a State, another Territory or New Zealand.
@ref s 121 (6), definition of government (src:1595-1595)
GIVEN subject IS A `Who or what an Act is applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 (6): the subject is a government` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `an Australian citizen` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a person who is not an Australian citizen` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the Territory (as a government)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Commonwealth (as a government)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a State (as a government)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another Territory (as a government)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `New Zealand (as a government)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `anyone or anything else` THEN NOTHING

-- The note under s 121 (1) points to a provision of another law about the Crown in right of the Commonwealth; it is not part of the Act (s 127 (1)).
-- src:1582 | (1) An Act binds everyone, including people who are not Australian citizens and all governments.
-- src:1583 | Note See the Self-Government Act, s 27 which provides that, except as provided by the regulations under that Act, an ACT enactment does not bind the Crown in right of the Commonwealth. See also s 120.
@ref s 121 (1) (src:1582-1583)
-- src:1584 | (2) However, an Act does not bind the Territory to the extent that it requires or otherwise provides for the payment of money that, on payment, would form part of the public money of the Territory.
@ref s 121 (2) (src:1584-1584)
GIVEN subject IS A `Who or what an Act is applied to`, theRequirementIsForPaymentOfMoneyThatOnPaymentWouldFormPartOfThePublicMoneyOfTheTerritory IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 (1), (2): the Act binds the subject` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `the Territory (as a government)` THEN
        IF   theRequirementIsForPaymentOfMoneyThatOnPaymentWouldFormPartOfThePublicMoneyOfTheTerritory
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1585 | (3) Also, subsection (1) does not make a government liable to be prosecuted for an offence.
@ref s 121 (3) (src:1585-1585)
GIVEN subject IS A `Who or what an Act is applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 (3): subsection (1) makes the subject liable to be prosecuted for an offence` MEANS
    IF   `s 121 (6): the subject is a government` subject EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Kinds of entity that s 121 (6) mentions.
-- `some other kind of entity` stands for an entity the definitions do not name.
-- src:1590 | authorised—an act or omission of a government entity is authorised if—
-- src:1591 | (a) for an instrumentality—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the instrumentality’s functions; and
-- src:1592 | (b) for an officer or employee of the government—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the duties of the officer or employee; and
-- src:1593 | (c) for a contractor who exercises a function on behalf of the government—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the contract; and
-- src:1594 | (d) for anyone else who exercises a function on behalf of the government—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the person’s engagement.
@ref s 121 (6), definition of authorised (src:1590-1594)
-- src:1596 | government entity includes—
-- src:1597 | (a) an instrumentality, officer or employee of the government; and
-- src:1598 | (b) a contractor or anyone else who exercises a function on behalf of the government.
@ref s 121 (6), definition of government entity (src:1596-1598)
DECLARE `Kind of entity of a government` IS ONE OF
    `an instrumentality of the government`
    `an officer or employee of the government`
    `a contractor who exercises a function on behalf of the government`
    `anyone else who exercises a function on behalf of the government`
    `some other kind of entity`

-- src:1596 | government entity includes—
-- src:1597 | (a) an instrumentality, officer or employee of the government; and
-- src:1598 | (b) a contractor or anyone else who exercises a function on behalf of the government.
@ref s 121 (6), definition of government entity (src:1596-1598)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity of a government`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 (6): the entity is a government entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an instrumentality of the government` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an officer or employee of the government` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a contractor who exercises a function on behalf of the government` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `anyone else who exercises a function on behalf of the government` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other kind of entity` THEN NOTHING

-- "authorised" is defined with a dash, "X is authorised if", and each paragraph names the kind of entity it is about.
-- It is read as a definition (JUST FALSE when the paragraph for the entity's kind is not met).
-- src:1590 | authorised—an act or omission of a government entity is authorised if—
-- src:1591 | (a) for an instrumentality—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the instrumentality’s functions; and
-- src:1592 | (b) for an officer or employee of the government—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the duties of the officer or employee; and
-- src:1593 | (c) for a contractor who exercises a function on behalf of the government—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the contract; and
-- src:1594 | (d) for anyone else who exercises a function on behalf of the government—the act or omission relates to a matter within the scope of the person’s engagement.
@ref s 121 (6), definition of authorised (src:1590-1594)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity of a government`, theActOrOmissionRelatesToAMatterWithinTheScopeOfTheEntitysFunctionsDutiesContractOrEngagement IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 (6): the act or omission of the government entity is authorised` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an instrumentality of the government` THEN JUST theActOrOmissionRelatesToAMatterWithinTheScopeOfTheEntitysFunctionsDutiesContractOrEngagement
    WHEN `an officer or employee of the government` THEN JUST theActOrOmissionRelatesToAMatterWithinTheScopeOfTheEntitysFunctionsDutiesContractOrEngagement
    WHEN `a contractor who exercises a function on behalf of the government` THEN JUST theActOrOmissionRelatesToAMatterWithinTheScopeOfTheEntitysFunctionsDutiesContractOrEngagement
    WHEN `anyone else who exercises a function on behalf of the government` THEN JUST theActOrOmissionRelatesToAMatterWithinTheScopeOfTheEntitysFunctionsDutiesContractOrEngagement
    WHEN `some other kind of entity` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1586 | (4) To the extent that an Act does not bind a government, the same degree of immunity extends to a government entity in relation to an authorised act or omission of the entity.
@ref s 121 (4) (src:1586-1586)
GIVEN theActDoesNotBindTheGovernmentToSomeExtent IS A BOOLEAN, theEntityIsAGovernmentEntity IS A BOOLEAN, theActOrOmissionOfTheEntityIsAuthorised IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 (4): the same degree of immunity extends to the government entity` MEANS
    IF   theActDoesNotBindTheGovernmentToSomeExtent AND theEntityIsAGovernmentEntity AND theActOrOmissionOfTheEntityIsAuthorised
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 122: Application to Territory`

-- src:1601 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument—
@ref s 122 (1) opening words (src:1601-1601)
-- src:1602 | (a) a reference to an entity or position by name or description is a reference to the entity or position of that name or description in or for the Territory; and
@ref s 122 (1) (a) (src:1602-1602)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnActOrStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsToAnEntityOrPositionByNameOrDescription IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122 (1) (a): the reference is a reference to the entity or position of that name or description in or for the Territory` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnActOrStatutoryInstrument AND theReferenceIsToAnEntityOrPositionByNameOrDescription
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1601 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument—
@ref s 122 (1) opening words (src:1601-1601)
-- src:1603 | (b) a reference to a place, jurisdiction or anything else by name or description is a reference to the place, jurisdiction or thing of that name or description in or for the Territory.
@ref s 122 (1) (b) (src:1603-1603)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnActOrStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsToAPlaceJurisdictionOrAnythingElseByNameOrDescription IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122 (1) (b): the reference is a reference to the place, jurisdiction or thing of that name or description in or for the Territory` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnActOrStatutoryInstrument AND theReferenceIsToAPlaceJurisdictionOrAnythingElseByNameOrDescription
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1604 | (2) If the name of an entity or position established under an Act or statutory instrument includes the words ‘of the Australian Capital Territory’, ‘for the Australian Capital Territory’, ‘(ACT)’, or words having a similar effect, a reference in an Act or statutory instrument to the entity or position need not include the words.
@ref s 122 (2) (src:1604-1604)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnActOrStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, theNameOfTheEntityOrPositionIncludesTheWordsOrWordsHavingASimilarEffect IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122 (2): the reference must include the words` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnActOrStatutoryInstrument AND theNameOfTheEntityOrPositionIncludesTheWordsOrWordsHavingASimilarEffect
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
